# Project Overview

This repository is a static HTML puzzle website — no build system, no framework, no dependencies. Each puzzle is a self-contained `.html` file with inline CSS and JS for puzzle-specific layout only. Shared styling and icons live in central assets. The site is opened directly in a browser from the filesystem.

```
puzzles/
├── index.html
├── styles/playful.css          ← active shared design system (Playful Geometric)
├── styles/old/neumorphic.css   ← archived dark neumorphic (unmigrated puzzles)
├── js/lucide.min.js            ← vendored Lucide icons (v0.468.0)
├── js/icons.js                 ← icon helper (initIcons, iconEl)
└── puzzles/                    ← puzzle .html files
```

**Design system transition:** The index and new/migrated puzzles use `styles/playful.css` (Playful Geometric — light cream, hard shadows, chunky borders). Unmigrated puzzles still link `../styles/old/neumorphic.css` until they are updated one-by-one. Prefer `playful.css` for any new work.

# Adding a New Puzzle

When asked to create a new puzzle, produce both:

1. A complete `puzzles/<puzzle_name>.html` file following the design system below.
2. An entry for the `puzzles` array in `index.html` (inside the clearly marked `ADD NEW PUZZLES HERE` block).

For `releaseDate`, default to the **later** of:

- the Friday after the current latest `releaseDate`, or
- the next Friday on or after today (if today is Friday, today counts).

In other words: keep the weekly Friday cadence, but never assign a date in the past. Override only if explicitly told otherwise.

# Shared Assets

Every page must link the shared assets. From `index.html` (and migrated puzzles):

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/playful.css" />
<script src="js/lucide.min.js"></script>
<script src="js/icons.js"></script>
```

From unmigrated puzzle pages under `puzzles/` (temporary):

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles/old/neumorphic.css" />
<script src="../js/lucide.min.js"></script>
<script src="../js/icons.js"></script>
```

Migrated puzzles should use `../styles/playful.css` instead.

Every puzzle page uses a themed body, ambient background, and back navigation:

```html
<body data-theme="link">
  <div class="ambient-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <main class="container container-narrow">
    <a href="../index.html" class="back-nav">
      <i data-lucide="arrow-left" class="icon icon-sm icon-themed"></i> All Puzzles
    </a>
    ...
```

Set `data-theme` to the same Lucide icon name used for that puzzle (e.g. `shuffle`, `link`, `brain`). The index page uses `data-theme="collection"`.

Call `PuzzleIcons.initIcons()` after DOM ready (and after any dynamic icon injection).

# Design System — Playful Geometric (active) / Neumorphism (archived)

**Active system:** Playful Geometric in `styles/playful.css` — warm cream paper (`#FFFDF5`), slate foreground (`#1E293B`), vivid violet accent (`#8B5CF6`), hard offset shadows (no blur), chunky 2px borders, Outfit headings + Plus Jakarta Sans body. Index already uses this; migrate puzzles to it over time.

**Archived:** Dark neumorphism remains in `styles/old/neumorphic.css` for unmigrated puzzles only. Details below still describe that archived look until those pages are converted.

## Core tokens (archived neumorphic — do not use for new work)

- **Background:** `#232936` — dark cool-grey page surface (`--bg`)
- **Cards / chrome:** `#2C3342` — slightly elevated surface (`--surface`)
- **Foreground:** `#EDF0F5` — primary text
- **Muted:** `#9AA5B5` — secondary text
- **Accent:** `#6C63FF` — CTAs and focus states only (not headings)
- **Success:** `#38B2AC` — correct/success states
- **Fonts:** Plus Jakarta Sans (display headings), DM Sans (body) — loaded via `neumorphic.css`
- **Container radius:** `32px` — **Button/input radius:** `16px`
- **Shadows:** dual RGBA shadows only (never opaque hex shadows, never borders)
- **Transitions:** `300ms ease-out`

## Anti-patterns

- No flat buttons — always use extruded/inset shadows
- No `rounded-lg` or sharper — minimum `16px` on interactive elements
- No emoji for UI iconography — use Lucide icons
- No gradient text on headings — use `#3D4852` display type
- All interactive elements need visible accent focus rings

## Page structure

```html
<body>
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <div class="card card-extruded">
      <header class="header">...</header>
      <!-- puzzle content -->
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
```

## Heading with Lucide icon in inset well

```html
<h1 class="font-display">
  <span class="icon-well icon-well-md"><i data-lucide="link" class="icon icon-md icon-themed"></i></span>
  <span class="title-text">Puzzle Title</span>
</h1>
```

Use the `icon-themed` class on decorative Lucide icons so they pick up each page's `--theme-color`.

## Icons

- UI/decorative icons: **Lucide** via `data-lucide="icon-name"` (kebab-case)
- Dynamic icons: `PuzzleIcons.iconEl("shuffle", { size: 32 })`
- Gameplay emojis in Einstein's Riddle and Nine Cats are intentionally preserved — do not replace those

## Required puzzle chrome

- **Timer:** starts on page load, displayed prominently, formatted as `M:SS` (no milliseconds)
- **Rules:** always visible on screen (no modal to hide them) — use `.rules` or `.rules-panel`
- **Winner modal:** triggered on completion; Lucide `party-popper` or `trophy` icon (not emoji), completion time in large text, "Close" and "Reset & Play Again" buttons using `.btn` / `.btn-primary` / `.btn-secondary`
- **Mobile:** full touchscreen support, minimum 44px touch targets

## Buttons and inputs

```html
<button class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
<button class="btn btn-secondary">Clear</button>
<input class="input" type="text" placeholder="..." />
```

## Feedback states

Use `.state-correct` and `.state-incorrect` on neumorphic surfaces with semantic teal/red tints — no hard borders.

# index.html Puzzle Registration

Each entry in the `puzzles` array:

```js
{
  title: "...",
  icon: "shuffle", // Lucide icon name (kebab-case), must be unique per puzzle
  description: "...", // 1-2 sentences, enticing but no spoilers
  file: "puzzles/...", // snake_case .html filename under the puzzles/ folder
  releaseDate: "YYYY-MM-DD",
}
```

Puzzles with a future `releaseDate` are hidden from the grid and replaced with a single "Coming Soon" card showing the next release date.

# Workflow

Do **not** read existing puzzle files when creating a new one. All necessary patterns are documented in this specification alone. Use inline `<style>` only for puzzle-specific layout (grids, custom shapes, etc.) — never duplicate shared tokens or base components.
